conch.app carries conch Microphone as Contents/Helpers/conch-microphone: the
microphone recorder of Sea Shell (https://github.com/stupart/seashell), built
from its source file native/macos-microphone.swift. conch runs it as a separate
program to capture the microphone.

Sea Shell is distributed under the MIT License: see LICENSE beside this notice,
unmodified from the Sea Shell source tree.

conch's copy of the source is mac-app/helpers/microphone/conch-microphone.swift
in conch's source, generated by scripts/sync-microphone.sh. Its first lines name
the Sea Shell commit and the sha256 of the file it was made from; only the
helper's identity was changed (its responsibility variable, usage line, error
domain and permission message), so that it holds conch's own Microphone
permission rather than Sea Shell's.
